[{:adr/id "2607122100"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-6201 (Computer programming activities, HubSpot Marketing Hub/Salesforce Marketing Cloud-class marketing-automation actor) deepened to :implemented"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-6201"
  :adr/related ["2607121900-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-crm-coverage (direct sibling, full-parity roadmap source)" "cloud-itonami-isic-7310 (advertising-agency actor, distinguished from)" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage (double-guard lesson source)" "kotoba-lang/crm (kotoba.crm.leadscore added in this build)"]
  :adr/narrowing "ISIC 6201 (Computer programming activities, broad n.e.c.) narrowed to a marketing-automation SaaS platform business (HubSpot Marketing Hub/Salesforce Marketing Cloud-class), explicitly distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-7310 (an advertising-AGENCY services actor, AdOps-LLM ⊣ Campaign Governor -- buys/places ads for clients) and from cloud-itonami-isic-5820 (sales/subscription-commerce CRM, a separate business-model sibling per the owner's per-business-model actor-split directive, not merged in)"
  :adr/pattern-6201 "sealed MarketingOps-LLM advisor + independent ConsentGovernor + append-only audit ledger, second sibling actor in the CRM/marketing/service-hub family after cloud-itonami-isic-5820, reusing kotoba-lang/crm's technical commons"
  :adr/distinctive-checks-6201 "consent-revoked-send-gate (HARD) is a genuinely new check kind for this fleet: an authorization-to-contact validity check (distinct from arithmetic, party-screening/independence, engagement-type, entitlement-scope, and stage-sequence check kinds already in this fleet's vocabulary). Rejects sending to a contact whose :consent-status is not :opted-in or whose :unsubscribed? flag is set, citing CAN-SPAM Act 15 U.S.C. §7704 (unsubscribe honoring, sender identification), EU GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) + Art. 7 (consent as a withdrawable lawful basis), and Canada's CASL S.C. 2010 c.23 (express/implied consent, mandatory unsubscribe mechanism) -- real, never-fabricated regulatory citations."
  :adr/guard-design-6201 "double-send-gate uses a dedicated :sent? boolean fact per (campaign, contact) pairing rather than a :status value, the same design discipline as cloud-itonami-isic-5820's double-close-gate, informed by cloud-itonami-isic-6920's status-lifecycle bug (ADR-2607071351). consent-revoked-send-gate likewise uses dedicated :consent-status/:unsubscribed? facts, never inferred from :lifecycle-stage."
  :adr/reused-commons "stage-sequence-gate reuses kotoba-lang/crm's kotoba.crm.pipeline directly (not reimplemented) for the lead lifecycle ([:subscriber :lead :mql :sql :customer], exit-stages #{:unsubscribed :bounced :disqualified}). lead-score-mismatch (SOFT, always-escalate) uses a NEW kotoba-lang/crm module added in this build, kotoba.crm.leadscore -- a fixed weighted-point ground-truth recompute (email-open=1, email-click=3, pricing-page-view=5, form-fill=10, demo-request=20), explicitly documented as this namespace's own invented spec since no external standard-setter exists for lead-scoring weights (unlike revrec's citable ASC 606/IFRS 15)."
  :adr/second-crm-commons-consumer "kotoba-lang/crm gains its second consumer after cloud-itonami-isic-5820, validating the owner's 'business-model-per-actor, technical-commons-in-kotoba-lang' split: kotoba.crm.pipeline was reused as-is with zero reimplementation"
  :adr/full-parity-roadmap-update "R0 scope for this actor is send/stage-transition/score-update core only -- no multi-step nurture sequence automation, no A/B testing, no landing-page builder. customer-service hub (Salesforce Service Cloud/HubSpot Service Hub-class) remains an unbuilt future sibling, named in cloud-itonami-isic-6201's own docs/adr/0001-architecture.md, per the same narrow-and-iterate discipline as ADR-2607121900"
  :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 142}"
  :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 143}"
  :adr/landing-method "kotoba-lang/industry registry+test update landed via the same atomic single-commit GitHub Git Data API method established in ADR-2607121900 (conditional ref update against exact tip SHA), succeeding on the first attempt this time"
  :adr/test-status-6201 "kotoba-lang/crm (leadscore addition): 16 tests / 52 assertions, 0 failures, lint 0 errors/0 warnings, commit e89d90672524c47153747415733a39ef425a1382. cloud-itonami-isic-6201: 31 tests / 114 assertions, 0 failures, lint 0 errors/0 warnings, sim run (10 demo ops) verified clean send/stage-advance/score-match commits plus correct rejection of opted-out/expired/unsubscribed sends, double-send, stage-skip, unauthorized role, and correct escalation on lead-score mismatch. A test-design bug (looping phase-gate assertions over phases where :lead/update-score isn't yet enabled at phase 1) was caught and fixed during test-authoring itself, before any test run -- not a shipped defect. commit b6cad1bb0e77c222f4d58092ee4d308ae7249fdd, pushed to github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6201."
  :adr/repos-published ["https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6201"]
  :adr/scope-note "This is a NEW ADR, not an addendum to ADR-2607121900, because ISIC 6201 is a distinct classification from 5820 with its own narrowing rationale and check-kind additions, even though it shares the identical governed-actor pattern and directly reuses ADR-2607121900's kotoba-lang/crm technical commons"}]
